WEBVTT


00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.040
Everyone talks about Korean skincare,

00:00:02.300 --> 00:00:05.660
but Japanese beauty has some of the best products in the world.

00:00:05.661 --> 00:00:08.381
Let me put you on to my favorite Japanese skin here.

00:00:08.382 --> 00:00:11.581
The Hada Labo Gokujun Toner is Japan's No. 1 toner.

00:00:11.582 --> 00:00:14.461
It's packed with multiple types of hyaluronic acid

00:00:14.462 --> 00:00:16.101
so your skin just soaks it up.

00:00:16.102 --> 00:00:17.701
Get this, if you have dehydrated,

00:00:17.702 --> 00:00:20.741
normal or combo skin, Senka's Perfect Whip Cleanser

00:00:20.742 --> 00:00:23.461
is a cleanser that you'll see in every Japanese drugstore.

00:00:23.462 --> 00:00:27.161
It creates the fluffiest cloud like foam to deeply cleanse your pores.

00:00:27.300 --> 00:00:29.660
Get this, if you have normal or oily skin,

00:00:29.661 --> 00:00:30.021
the

00:00:30.022 --> 00:00:33.901
SK2 Essence is probably one of the most iconic products of all time.

00:00:33.902 --> 00:00:35.741
It's famous for smoothing texture,

00:00:35.742 --> 00:00:38.341
brightening the skin and making your skin clear.

00:00:38.342 --> 00:00:39.581
Get this, if you have dark,

00:00:39.582 --> 00:00:41.581
ill, uneven or aging skin.

00:00:41.582 --> 00:00:46.261
And finally, the Biore Aqua Rich Sunscreen is Japan's No. 1 sunscreen

00:00:46.262 --> 00:00:48.141
year after year. It's lightweight,

00:00:48.142 --> 00:00:50.581
invisible and gives zero cast.

00:00:50.582 --> 00:00:53.301
Get this, if you have oily or combo skin.

00:00:53.302 --> 00:00:55.221
Japanese skincare can be hard to find,

00:00:55.222 --> 00:00:57.964
but you can find all of these and more at Kiyoko.
